JARVIS v8 - INSTALLATION CHECKLIST (Windows 10/11)
====================================================
Do these steps IN ORDER before running jarvis.py.


STEP 0 - SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
-----------------------------
[ ] Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit)
[ ] Python 3.12 installed (https://www.python.org/downloads/)
      - During install, CHECK "Add python.exe to PATH"
[ ] At least 8 GB free RAM (16 GB recommended) for local AI models
[ ] At least 10 GB free disk space (for Ollama models)
[ ] Working microphone and speakers
[ ] Internet connection (for speech recognition + weather/news)


STEP 1 - WINDOWS PRIVACY PERMISSIONS
--------------------------------------
[ ] Settings > Privacy & Security > Microphone
      - "Microphone access" = ON
      - "Let apps access your microphone" = ON
      - "Let desktop apps access your microphone" = ON


STEP 2 - INSTALL OLLAMA
-------------------------
[ ] Download and install: https://ollama.com/download/windows
[ ] Open a terminal and run:
      ollama pull qwen3:8b
      ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b
[ ] Keep the Ollama app/service running in the background whenever
    Jarvis is running (check the system tray).


STEP 3 - INSTALL TESSERACT OCR
---------------------------------
[ ] Run in PowerShell:
      winget install --exact --id UB-Mannheim.TesseractOCR
[ ] Confirm it installed to:
      C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe
[ ] Download Hindi language data (needed for Hindi OCR/on-screen text
    matching) from:
      https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata/raw/main/hin.traineddata
[ ] Place hin.traineddata in:
      C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tessdata\


STEP 4 - INSTALL PYTHON PACKAGES
-----------------------------------
[ ] Open the project folder in a terminal and run:

python -m pip install customtkinter feedparser mss numpy ollama psutil PyAutoGUI PyAudio pyperclip pytesseract requests screen-brightness-control SpeechRecognition Pillow pywin32 pystray edge-tts

[ ] If PyAudio fails to install, try:
      pip install pipwin
      pipwin install pyaudio

[ ] After installation finishes, verify pywin32 registered correctly:
      python -c "import win32com.client; print('pywin32 OK')"
    If this errors, run:
      python Scripts\pywin32_postinstall.py -install
    (path may vary; find it inside your Python install's Scripts folder)


STEP 5 - VERIFY edge-playback (HINDI VOICE)
----------------------------------------------
[ ] Open a NEW terminal (so PATH refreshes) and run:
      edge-playback --help
[ ] If "command not found":
      - Find your Python Scripts folder, e.g.:
          C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python312\Scripts
      - Add it to your Windows PATH environment variable
      - Reopen terminal and test again


STEP 6 - FINAL CHECKS BEFORE RUNNING
----------------------------------------
[ ] Ollama app is running (check system tray icon)
[ ] Run: ollama list
      -> should show qwen3:8b and qwen2.5vl:7b
[ ] Tesseract path confirmed: C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe
[ ] Microphone permissions enabled (Step 1)
[ ] All pip packages installed with no errors


STEP 7 - RUN JARVIS
-----------------------
[ ] python jarvis.py
      (replace "jarvis.py" with your actual filename)


TROUBLESHOOTING QUICK REFERENCE
-----------------------------------
- "I could not connect to Ollama"        -> Ollama app not running, or model not pulled
- Hindi speech doesn't play               -> edge-playback not on PATH (see Step 5)
- Hindi text not detected on screen       -> hin.traineddata missing (see Step 3)
- Microphone not detected / silent fails  -> Check Windows privacy settings (Step 1)
- PyAudio install fails                   -> Use pipwin (see Step 4)
- win32com / SAPI errors                  -> Run pywin32 postinstall script (Step 4)
- Everything is very slow                 -> Not enough RAM for the 8B models
